  劳燕分飞 | láo yàn fēn fēi | part ways like swallows flying in opposite directions
  一别两宽 | yì bié liǎng kuān | part company and wish each other peace and freedom
  各奔前程 | gè bèn qián chéng | each goes their own separate way towards the future
  破镜重圆 | pò jìng chóng yuán | a broken mirror joined together again; reunite after estrangement

character_decomposition[2]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,meaning_es,radical,radical_meaning_en,meaning_component,sound_component,stroke_count,composition_type,etymology_and_mnemonic,visual_mnemonic_story_en,visual_mnemonic_story_es,tone_mnemonic_anchor,cangjie,traditional}:
  离 | lí | leave; depart; separate; distance | separarse; alejarse; distancia; partir | 亠 | lid | 禸 (animal footstep departing) | 离 (lí, mythological bird) | 10 | 上下结构 | Anciently depicted an oriolar bird caught in a net that frees itself and takes flight away. | A bird trapped under a canopy (亠) spreads its wings, leaving footmarks behind (禸) as it parts forever. | Un ave atrapada bajo un cobertizo (亠) alza el vuelo dejando huellas (禸) al partir para siempre. | 35 | YUBB | 離
  婚 | hūn | marry; wedding; marriage | casarse; boda; matrimonio | 女 | woman | 女 (woman, the bride entering home) | 昏 (hūn, dusk/evening wedding rites) | 11 | 左右结构 | Ideogram of taking a bride (女) home at twilight dusk (昏), the auspicious time for ancient nuptials. | The bride (女) is escorted to her new home right as the sun sets at dusk (昏). | La novia (女) es recibida en su nuevo hogar justo cuando el sol se oculta en el crepúsculo (昏). | 55 | VHPA | ""

mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Separating (离) from the marital bonds forged at dusk (婚) legally dissolves the union.
  composite_memory_hook_es: Separarse (离) del vínculo matrimonial sellado en el crepúsculo (婚) constituye el divorcio legal.
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: Marriage in traditional China was a sacred cosmic and lineage union celebrated at dusk (昏); 'lí' (departure) paired with 'hūn' marks the institutional and emotional severing of this social bond.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: 35-55 pitch contour. The rising 2nd tone of lí ascends smoothly to meet the steady high level tone of hūn (55).

traps_and_cognates:
  look_alikes[4]{character,pinyin,meaning_en,distinction_note}:
    禽 | qín | bird; fowl | Features 人 at the top instead of 亠; bottom has different interior
    篱 | lí | bamboo fence | Has bamboo radical 竹 on top of 离
    昏 | hūn | dusk; faint | Lacks the woman radical 女 on the left
    姻 | yīn | marriage by affinity | Has 因 on the right rather than 昏
  etymological_cognates[4]{character,pinyin,gloss_en}:
    别 | bié | part; separate; sharing departure nuance
    分 | fēn | divide; split into parts
    嫁 | jià | marry off a woman in the 女 radical cluster
    娶 | qǔ | take a wife

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 离婚 specifically and exclusively refers to the formal or legal dissolution of a registered marriage.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 离婚 vs. 分手 | fēnshǒu | 分手 is broadly applied to boyfriends, girlfriends, dating couples, or business partners breaking up, whereas 离婚 strictly requires legal marriage dissolution.
    2 | 离婚 vs. 分居 | fēnjū | 分居 means living apart in separate residences while remaining legally married, whereas 离婚 dissolves marital status entirely.
    3 | 离婚 vs. 绝交 | juéjiāo | 绝交 refers to severing social ties or friendship between friends or associates, unrelated to matrimonial law.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 婚姻走到尽头并不意味着人生的彻底失败。选择离婚，有时是双方在认清彼此无法同行后，给予对方最体面的解脱。带着理智与温和告别过去，勇敢开始独立的生活，同样是对生命的真诚交代。 | Hūnyīn zǒudào jìntóu bìng bù yìwèizhe rénshēng de chèdǐ shībài. Xuǎnzé líhūn, yǒushí shì shuāngfāng zài rènqīng bǐcǐ wúfǎ tóngxíng hòu, jǐyǔ duìfāng zuì tǐmiàn de jiětuō. Dàizhe lǐzhì yǔ wēnhé gàobié guòqù, yǒnggǎn kāishǐ dúlì de shēnghuó, tóngyàng shì duì shēngmìng de zhēnchéng jiāodài. | The end of a marriage does not signify absolute personal defeat. Choosing divorce is sometimes the most dignified release after realizing that paths diverge. Saying farewell with rationality and beginning life anew is a sincere tribute to living. | Que un matrimonio llegue a su fin no implica un fracaso absoluto. Divorciarse es a veces la salida más digna tras comprender que los caminos se bifurcan. Despedirse con serenidad para emprender una vida independiente es un acto de honestidad vital.
  #2 | 随着社会经济结构演变与女性经济独立性的提高，当代社会的离婚观念呈现出理性化趋势。法律学者指出，健全的离婚财产分割机制与未成年子女探望保障，对于缓解单亲家庭抚育压力具有深远意义。 | Suízhe shèhuì jīngjì jiégòu yǎnbiàn yǔ nǚxìng jīngjì dúlìxìng de tígāo, dāngdài shèhuì de líhūn guānniàn chéngxiàn chū lǐxìnghuà qūshì. Fǎxué xuézhě zhǐchū, jiànquán de líhūn cáichǎn fēngē jīzhì yǔ wèichéngnián zǐnǚ tànwàng bǎozhàng, duìyú huǎnjiě dānqīn jiātíng fǔyù yālì jùyǒu shēnyuǎn yìyì. | With evolving economic structures and women's growing autonomy, modern views on divorce have become rationalized. Legal scholars note that sound property division and child visitation safeguards are vital to alleviating pressure on single-parent homes. | Con el desarrollo socioeconómico y la autonomía femenina, la concepción del divorcio se ha vuelto más racional. Los juristas destacan que mecanismos claros de división patrimonial y visitas protegen el bienestar de los hogares monoparentales.
